-Xms1g
-Xmx4g
-XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=1024m
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=1g
-Xss4M
# WORKAROUND: a HotSpot C2 miscompile on JDK 23+ (incl. Temurin 25.0.4.1):
# ReduceAllocationMerges can null a field read through a phi that merges a fresh
# allocation with an existing object (JDK-8385993, fixed in JDK 28; dup JDK-8393049).
# It intermittently crashed scaladoc 3.3.8 in `sbt dist` with an impossible NPE in
# SignatureBuilder.signature (content() == null). Scaladoc and scalac run in this
# sbt JVM, so the flag goes here. IgnoreUnrecognizedVMOptions keeps JDK 21 (which
# lacks the flag) starting; note it also hides typos in this file.
# Drop these three lines once the build JDK carries the JDK-8385993 fix.
-XX:+IgnoreUnrecognizedVMOptions
-XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions
-XX:-ReduceAllocationMerges
